const EN_METIN: string[] = [
  'We have just listened to the closing verses of Sūrat al-Baqara: words that close a long chapter the way one closes a door on doubt, and open a window onto certainty. They say something fundamental: faith is not a constraint, it is a free answer. God lays on no soul a burden greater than it can bear; He knows the limits of a human being better than that person knows them.',
  'You are here today not by accident, not under pressure, not out of weakness, but at the end of an inward journey — sometimes silent, sometimes painful, often solitary. Seeking the truth is never comfortable. It is a crossing, and every crossing worthy of the name has its questions, its ruptures, its fears, and its clear skies too.',
  'The Islam you are about to embrace is not a foreign culture, nor an ethnic belonging, nor an inherited tradition. Islam is first of all a recognition: recognising the absolute Oneness of God — the One, without partner, without intermediary, without incarnation; who does not beget and was not begotten; who resembles nothing the human mind can picture, yet is closer to you than your own breath.',
  'Entering Islam is not denying your past. It is not disowning your history, your identity, the road you have walked. It is giving that road a new meaning. Islam does not erase what you have been; it puts in order what you are becoming. It turns the search into a direction, doubt into responsibility, freedom into a conscious commitment.',
  'Know this above all: in Islam God does not look for angels, He welcomes human beings — imperfect, fragile, able to fall and able to rise. The door of repentance is never closed. Divine mercy is not earned by perfection; it is received through sincerity.',
  'In becoming a Muslim today you affirm that life is not absurd, that it is not left to chance, that it has an origin, a meaning and an end. You affirm that every act counts, that every word carries weight, that every intention has a value. You accept being answerable before God — not to be crushed by fear, but to be raised by conscience.',
  'Islam does not promise you a life without trials; it promises you a compass. It does not promise you the absence of pain; it promises pain a meaning. It does not promise that everything will be easy; it promises that nothing will be in vain.',
  'You will learn step by step. Faith is not a switch; it is a light that settles in. No one will ask you to be perfect from today. What God asks of you is honesty of heart and steadiness of step, however slow.',
  'From this moment you enter a brotherhood without borders, without a single colour, without an exclusive language — a fellowship founded on faith in God, on human dignity, on justice and on mercy. You are not alone. You are no longer alone.',
  'In a moment you will pronounce the word that has crossed centuries, deserts, empires and consciences: the testimony of faith. A short sentence, yet heavier than the mountains. A sentence that does not make you someone new in the eyes of people, but gives you a new birth before God.',
  'Say it with clarity, with calm, with conviction — not as a magic formula, but as a free commitment. And know that, according to the teaching of Islam, at the very moment you attest it sincerely your past is washed away: not by forgetting, but by mercy.',
  'May God make your heart firm, light your path, calm your worries, and make of you a person of uprightness, wisdom and peace.',
];

